 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Keep it simple. A short outdoor service at the cemetery, with a speech and music, is the most popular format. The couple can share something personal, a poem or a quote from the deceased. A friend or family member can give the speech. A simple ritual can be lovely. Lighting candle, tossing a handful of soil on casket, or standing in the sun for a moment are all easy touches. Lovely. A cherry blossom tree for spring, or something tough like a rose bush for the couple to look after. Something living that the animals will appreciate too.",
